<div class="img-note">
  <strong>🎨 Generating postcard images with Draw Things</strong><br/>
  Run Draw Things on your Mac with its <strong>Local Server</strong> mode enabled (defaults to <code>http://127.0.0.1:7860</code>).<br/>
  Then POST to its Stable Diffusion API:
  <pre style="margin:0.5rem 0 0; background:rgba(93,143,163,0.06); padding:0.75rem; border-radius:8px; font-size:0.78rem; overflow-x:auto;">curl http://127.0.0.1:7860/sdapi/v1/txt2img \
  -d '{"prompt":"vintage postcard...","width":1024,"height":768,"steps":20,"cfg_scale":6,"batch_size":1}'</pre>
  Full prompt + negative prompt + style suffixes are in
  <code>crustaceans-internal/drawthings-prompts.md</code>. Use the toolkit script
  <code>python crustaceans-internal/drawthings-generate.py &lt;slug&gt;</code> to generate, poll GPU idle, and promote the best output automatically.
</div>

